# Docsify links — NON-NEGOTIABLE

The site uses Docsify with **`relativePath: true`** in **`index.html`**. Docsify resolves every link against the **current hash route**, not against the file that contains the link.

## Why

- **`[Sound](sound.md)`** on **`#/reference/README`** becomes **`#/sound`** (404) unless **`relativePath: true`** and the link is a same-folder sibling.
- **`[Audio](/manuals/audio.md)`** in **`_sidebar.md`** is required. With **`relativePath: true`**, a sidebar target **`manuals/audio.md`** (no leading slash) from **`#/manuals/index`** becomes **`#/manuals/manuals/audio`** (404).

## Rules

1. **Same folder (page body):** filename only. On **`manuals/audio.md`**: **`[Sound component](audio_sound_component.md)`**.
2. **Cross folder (page body):** **`../`**. On **`manuals/audio.md`**: **`[Sound](../reference/sound.md)`**.
3. **`_sidebar.md` and root `README.md`:** always a **leading slash** from the site root. Examples: **`/manuals/audio.md`**, **`/getting_started/faq.md`**, **`/reference/README.md`**, **`/README.md`**. Never **`manuals/audio.md`** without **`/`** in the sidebar.
4. **Inside a content folder**, do not repeat that folder name. On **`getting_started/faq.md`**, use **`installation.md`**, not **`getting_started/installation.md`**.
5. **Inside `reference/`**, group links on **`README.md`** use **`sound.md`**, not **`reference/sound.md`**.

## Script API index

**`tools/generate_script_api_reference.py`** (engine repo) emits **`({group}.md)`** on **`reference/README.md`**. If it touches **`_sidebar.md`**, the Script API entry must be **`/reference/README.md`**.

## When editing **`index.html`**

Keep **`relativePath: true`**. Do not remove it without another routing fix.

## Check before shipping

From **`#/manuals/audio`**, click **Manual** in the sidebar (expect **`#/manuals/index`**, not **`#/manuals/manuals/index`**). From **`#/reference/README`**, click **Sound** (expect **`#/reference/sound`**).
